module

public import ReasLib.RingTheory.Kaehler.SurjectiveSquare
import StacksCheckRecall

@[expose] public section

/-!
# Kaehler differentials of a surjective square

@stack 00RR

The source statement splits into Mathlib's canonical surjectivity theorem and the reusable
ReasLib kernel description.  The elementwise checks expose the two generator interfaces used by
later exact-sequence arguments.
-/

/- Lemma 10.131.6 (1): a surjective map in a commutative square induces a surjective map on
Kaehler differentials. -/
@[stacks 00RR "(1), surjectivity"]
#check @KaehlerDifferential.map_surjective_of_surjective

/- Lemma 10.131.6 (2): the kernel is generated by differentials of elements whose image comes
from the new base ring. -/
@[stacks 00RR "(2), kernel description"]
#check @KaehlerDifferential.ker_map_eq_span_of_surjective

/- The kernel description includes the differentials of elements in `ker (S → S')`. -/
@[stacks 00RR "kernel-element companion"]
#check @KaehlerDifferential.D_mem_ker_map_of_mem_ker

/- The more general elementwise API only requires the image to lie in the range of the new base
ring. -/
#check @KaehlerDifferential.D_mem_ker_map_of_map_mem_range
